\c 1
\rem /s1 Greetings from James; Salutation
\p
\v 1 \add This letter is from\add* Yacob, a slave¦146464 for \nd God¦146459\nd* and¦146460 for \add the\add* \nd master¦146461 Yeshua¦146462\nd* the \nd messiah¦146463\nd*. \add It's written\add* to¦146472 the tribes¦146467 who have ended up dispersed¦146471 \add into many nations\add*:\x + \xo 1:1: \xt Mat 13:55; Mrk 6:3; Acts 15:13; Gal 1:19.\x* Greetings¦146472.
\s1 Gaining endurance and requesting wisdom
\rem /s1 Faith and Wisdom; Faith and Endurance; Faith under trial; Trials and Temptations
\p
\v 2 Be cheerful¦146474 my¦146477 fellow¦146476 believers¦146476, when you¦146480 face a range¦146481 of¦146477 difficult situations,
\v 3 knowing¦146483 that¦146484 you¦146487 will learn endurance¦146491 as your¦146487 faith¦146489 is¦146490 tested.
\v 4 Let that endurance¦146494 do its¦146496 perfect work¦146495 so that you¦146499 all¦146499 might become perfect and¦146501 mature—not lacking¦146505 anything.
\p
\v 5 If¦146506 anyone¦146508 of¦146509 you is¦146510 lacking¦146510 wisdom¦146511, then it should¦146512 be requested¦146512 from¦146513 \nd God¦146518\nd* who gives¦146517 it generously¦146520 and without disparagement, and so it will¦146526 be given¦146526 to¦146527 you,
\v 6 but¦146529 the person who's asking should¦146528 demonstrate their faith¦146531 and not be doubting. That's because¦146535 a person who doubts is¦146537 like¦146537 a wave¦146538 on the sea¦146539 that's just blown¦146540 and tossed¦146542 around
\v 7 and a person¦146547 like that shouldn't¦146543 expect to get anything¦146551 from¦146552 the¦146553 \nd master¦146555\nd*
\rem /s1 Poverty and Riches
\v 8 because that person is double-minded¦146557, and everything they attempt ends up in¦146559 difficulty.
\s1 Behaviour of the poor and the wealthy
\p
\v 9 Those of¦146573 humbler¦146569 means can boast¦146564 about¦146573 their greatness
\v 10 whereas the wealthy¦146576 can boast about¦146581 their weakness because¦146582 they'll pass¦146586 away just like the daisies in the grass¦146585.\x + \xo 1:10-11: \xt Isa 40:6-7 (LXX).\x*
\v 11 When the sun¦146590 rises¦146587 with¦146591 its¦146601 scorching¦146593 heat¦146593 and withers¦146595 the grass¦146597, the flowers¦146600 will drop and lose all their beauty¦146605. So too for rich¦146613 people who'll fade away right in the middle of all their projects.
\s1 Testing and temptation
\rem /s1 Trial and Temptation; Testing and Tempting
\p
\v 12 Any person who's¦146623 enduring¦146624 testing circumstances is¦146624 fortunate, because¦146627 once they've passed the¦146631 test, they'll receive¦146630 a crown¦146632 of¦146634 life¦146634 that¦146635 Yeshua promised¦146636 to¦146639 those who love¦146640 him¦146641.
\v 13 No one¦146642 should¦146644 say¦146644 ‘It's God tempting¦146657 me’ when they're being¦146643 tempted, because¦146652 God can't be¦146644 tempted to do evil¦146656 and¦146658 he¦146659 doesn't tempt¦146657 others,
\v 14 but¦146662 rather they're being tempted¦146663 by¦146664 their own¦146666 lusts. They're being drawn¦146668 away¦146668 and¦146669 enticed¦146670 \add into what they know is wrong\add*,
\v 15 and after the desire¦146673 is conceived¦146674 it leads to sin, and once the sin is concluded it leads to death¦146682.
\p
\v 16 Don't be¦146684 led astray, my¦146686 dear¦146687 brothers¦146685 and¦146685 sisters¦146685.
\v 17 Every¦146688 gift¦146693 that's good¦146690 and¦146691 perfect¦146694 comes from heaven. It comes down¦146697 from the¦146700 father¦146701 of lights¦146703, none of which are changing or casting moving shadows¦146713.
\v 18 Once he had decided it¦146715, he created us¦146717 by¦146718 his spoken commands so that we'd become a kind of special first¦146724 ‘harvest’ out of all of his creatures¦146729.
\s1 Listening then doing
\rem /s1 Hearing and Doing the Word; Listening and Doing
\p
\v 19 So my¦146735 dear¦146736 brothers¦146734 and sisters¦146734, note this: Everyone should be quick¦146743 to listen¦146746 but¦146740 slow to speak¦146750, and should be slow to get angry
\v 20 because¦146755 when people get very angry, it doesn't lead to the good behaviour that \nd God¦146758\nd* expects.
\v 21 So¦146762 discard all \add moral\add* filth¦146765 and the evil¦146769 that's plentiful, and humbly accept the message¦146776 that's implanted¦146775 in you¦146782 all¦146782 and which is capable of¦146782 saving¦146779 your¦146782 souls¦146781.
\p
\v 22 Don't¦146788 delude¦146792 yourselves¦146793 by just listening¦146790 to the¦146786 message¦146786, but¦146784 put it into practice \add in your daily lives\add*.
\v 23 Anyone¦146796 who is just a listener¦146797 of¦146798 the¦146798 message¦146798 and¦146800 does nothing with it is like¦146804 someone¦146796 who looks at their face¦146809 in¦146813 a mirror¦146814
\v 24 but¦146818 goes¦146819 away¦146819 after having¦146819 a look and¦146820 then immediately¦146821 forgets¦146822 what¦146823 they looked like.
\v 25 However the person who investigates¦146827 the perfect¦146830 law that gives freedom¦146833, and¦146834 then sticks with¦146835 it, not¦146837 being just an observer that forgets¦146839 about¦146833 it but¦146826 rather a person who puts it into practice, this¦146844 person will prosper in whatever they do¦146848.
\p
\v 26 If anyone¦146853 supposes¦146854 that they're religious¦146855 but¦146865 doesn't guard what comes out of their mouth, then that person's religion¦146874 is¦146872 only skin deep and hasn't affected their heart¦146867.
\v 27 A person who wants to truly serve our¦146881 \nd God¦146882\nd* and father¦146885 with a pure¦146877 heart would be¦146888 visiting¦146888 orphans¦146889 and widows¦146891 in¦146892 their¦146895 difficulties and staying unstained by worldly¦146903 ideas.
\c 2
\s1 Avoiding favouritism
