\v 1 My¦146905 dear brothers¦146904 and¦146904 sisters¦146904, as you live out your faith¦146911 in our¦146914 honoured \nd master¦146913 Yeshua¦146915\nd* the \nd messiah¦146916\nd*, don't¦146906 show favouritism¦146908 to others.
\v 2 For \add example\add*, if¦146919 a man in nicely cut clothes and¦146932 wearing an expensive gold¦146927 ring¦146927 came into to your¦146925 meeting as well as a poor¦146934 man in filthy¦146936 clothes
\v 3 and¦146940 you¦146939 told the well-dressed one, ‘You sit here in this good¦146954 chair,’ while telling the poor¦146957 man, ‘You stand¦146960 over here,’ or¦146962 ‘You sit here on the mat,’
\v 4 wouldn't that discrimination show that you¦146976 have judged¦146981 them with¦146982 evil¦146983 motives.
\v 5 Listen my¦146986 dear¦146987 brothers¦146985 and sisters¦146985, didn't¦146988 \nd God¦146990\nd* chose¦146991 the poor¦146993 in this world¦146996 to be¦147001 rich¦146999 in faith¦147001 and participants in the kingdom¦147006 which¦147007 he¦147008 promises¦147008 to those who love¦147010 him¦147011?
