\v 8 However¦147042 if you are¦147044 obeying the golden law¦147043, then when you love¦147050 your¦147053 neighbour¦147052 as¦147054 yourself¦147055,\x + \xo 2:8: \xt Lev 19:18.\x* you'll be doing¦147061 well¦147060 according¦147047 to the scriptures¦147049.
\v 9 But if¦147062 you're showing¦147064 favouritism¦147064, then you're all sinning¦147065 by¦147068 breaking the¦147069 law¦147070.
\v 10 Because¦147075 anyone¦147087 who tries to keep¦147080 the law but¦147085 slips up in¦147086 one¦147087 area, they're still guilty of¦147089 breaking the law.
\v 11 The¦147091 same \add God\add* who said, ‘Don't commit¦147096 adultery,’ also said, ‘Don't murder,’\x + \xo 2:11: a \xt Exo 20:14; Deu 5:18; \xo b \xt Exo 20:13; Deu 5:17.\x* so if¦147104 you're¦147107 not¦147106 committing¦147107 adultery but¦147105 you murder someone, then¦147105 you've¦147112 broken the¦147116 law¦147116.
\v 12 So speak¦147118 and¦147119 live your life knowing that you're going¦147126 to¦147127 be¦147127 judged¦147127 by¦147123 the¦147124 law¦147124 that gives freedom¦147125,
\v 13 because¦147129 judgement will¦147131 be¦147131 dispensed without mercy to¦147132 those who haven't been putting mercy into practice. Yes, mercy wins out over¦147142 judgement.
\s1 Faith in action
