\p
\v 13 Any of you¦147638 that are wise¦147634 and understanding¦147636 should¦147639 demonstrate their good¦147642 deeds and wisdom¦147649 by their godly living.
\v 14 But¦147656 if¦147650 you¦147655 are¦147655 full of¦147663 bitter¦147654 jealousy¦147653 or selfish¦147657 ambition¦147657, don't¦147664 be boasting¦147666 or denying the¦147670 truth¦147671
\v 15 because none of that¦147676 came¦147681 down to you from heaven, but¦147682 on the contrary it's earthly¦147683 and soulish¦147684 and demonic¦147685.
\v 16 Wherever¦147686 you find jealousy¦147688 and selfish¦147690 ambition¦147690, you'll also find disharmony and all kinds of evil¦147697.
\v 17 In contrast, the¦147699 wisdom¦147702 that comes from¦147701 God is¦147706 pure¦147705, peaceable¦147708, gentle¦147709, compliant¦147710, full¦147711 of¦147712 mercy¦147712 and good¦147716 behaviour, unceasing¦147717, and not hypocritical.
\v 18 Those who desire peace¦147726 sow¦147727 \add the seeds\add* that will produce¦147720 godly behaviour.
\c 4
\s1 Don't befriend the world
\rem /s1 Submit Yourselves to God; Friendship with the World; Drawing Close to God
\p
\v 1 Where do you imagine that the fights and¦147735 quarrels¦147737 among¦147738 you¦147739 all¦147739 originate? Isn't it¦147740 because of¦147745 the ambitions that surface inside you?
\v 2 You¦147752 all¦147752 have wants that are¦147752 not fulfilled so it leads to murder¦147756. You're jealous¦147758 and not able¦147761 to get everything you want, so you quarrel¦147763 and fight. You don't¦147754 have, because¦147770 you haven't asked \add God\add*,
\v 3 and¦147776 when you¦147778 all¦147778 do ask, it¦147789 doesn't get answered because¦147779 you ask with wrong¦147780 \add motives\add*—trying get what you want to spend¦147789 on your¦147787 own wants.
\v 4 You're just like prostitutes. Don't you realise that¦147795 if you befriend the world then you're opposing God, so anyone who befriends the world makes themself an¦147818 enemy¦147818 of God.
\v 5 Do you¦147823 think that¦147835 the scripture¦147828 means nothing when it says¦147829, ‘\add God's\add* \nd spirit¦147834\nd* jealously longs to¦147836 live in¦147838 us¦147839’?
\v 6 However, he's¦147842 good at giving¦147842 grace so that's why it says¦147845, ‘\nd God¦147847\nd* opposes¦147849 proud¦147848 people but¦147841 gives grace to humble¦147850 ones.’\x + \xo 4:6: \xt Prv 3:34 (LXX).\x*
\v 7 So¦147855 strive then to do what \nd God¦147857\nd* wants of you. Resist¦147858 the devil¦147861 and¦147862 he¦147863 will¦147863 flee¦147863 away from¦147864 you.
\v 8 When you¦147871 all¦147871 approach God, he¦147870 will¦147870 move closer to¦147871 you. So keep your hands¦147873 clean you sinners¦147874, and¦147875 keep your hearts¦147877 pure you who can't make up your minds about God.
\v 9 Be miserable¦147879, and mourn¦147881 and weep¦147883. Change your laughing¦147885 into crying and your happiness into sadness
\v 10 because when you humble¦147896 yourselves towards \nd Yahweh¦147900\nd*, he¦147902 will¦147902 be¦147902 the one to lift you up.
\s1 Avoid judging others
\rem /s1 Warning against Judging Others; Warning against Judging Another; Warning against Judging One Another
\p
\v 11 My fellow believers¦147907, don't¦147929 make false accusations against each other because anyone¦147906 who falsely accuses or¦147913 judges a fellow believer, is¦147919 slandering¦147911 against the law and¦147921 judging it. But¦147921 if you're the ones judging the law, then you're not¦147929 a follower of the law but¦147926 a judge¦147934 of it.
\v 12 There's only one lawgiver¦147938 and judge and that's the¦147941 one who is able¦147942 to save¦147943 and to destroy¦147945. So who do you think you are¦147949 to judge your¦147954 neighbour¦147955!
\s1 Avoid boasting and presumption
