\p
\v 13 Now¦147958 you¦147959 all¦147959 might say¦147960, ‘Today¦147961 or¦147962 tomorrow¦147964 we'll¦147965 go¦147965 into¦147967 the¦147969 city¦147970 to work¦147972 there¦147974 for a year¦147975 and do some trading to make some money.’\x + \xo 4:13-14: \xt Prv 27:1.\x*
\v 14 But you don't¦147984 know¦147985 what tomorrow will¦147989 bring, because¦147991 what are¦147997 your¦147994 lives? You're like a vapour¦147995 that¦148000 appears¦148003 for¦148001 a brief period and then¦148004 it's gone.
\v 15 So instead of¦148008 saying¦148010 that, you¦148011 should¦148011 say, ‘If the¦148013 \nd master¦148014\nd* wants it, we will live¦148018 and¦148020 we'll¦148018 do¦148021 this¦148023 or¦148024 that.’
\v 16 But as it is¦148039, you've all¦148028 been boasting¦148036 in¦148030 your¦148033 arrogance¦148032 and that's an evil¦148038 attitude.
\v 17 Any person who knows¦148040 that there's some good¦148042 thing that they should be¦148043 doing, but¦148045 doesn't do it, is¦148050 sinning¦148048.
\c 5
