\p
\v 1 So you wealthy¦148055 people, come¦148051 and cry about the¦148059 miseries¦148060 that¦148062 are¦148062 about to hit you¦148053 all¦148053.
\v 2 Your¦148067 riches¦148066 have rotted¦148068 and¦148069 your¦148067 clothes¦148071 have become¦148074 moth-eaten¦148073.\x + \xo 5:2-3: \xt Mat 6:19.\x*
\v 3 Your¦148077 gold¦148076 and silver¦148081 has¦148082 corroded¦148082, and that corrosion will speak out against you and will eat away your¦148077 bodies like fire¦148100 because you stored¦148101 up¦148101 wealth in¦148102 this final age.
\v 4 The¦148107 unpaid wages of the workers¦148110 who harvested¦148112 your¦148115 fields¦148114 are crying¦148121 out\x + \xo 5:4: \xt Deu 24:14-15.\x* and¦148122 the desperate requests of those harvesters¦148112 have¦148132 been¦148117 heard by¦148119 army commander \nd Yahweh¦148130\nd*.
\v 5 You have indulged¦148134 yourselves and¦148139 lived¦148140 luxuriously¦148140 but¦148139 you've been fattening yourselves up as the time for your¦148144 slaughter¦148149 approaches.
\v 6 You¦148150 all¦148150 convicted¦148150 innocent people and had them executed, even when they weren't doing anything against¦148156 you.
\s1 Wait patiently
\rem /s1 Patience and Prayer; Patience in Suffering
\p
\v 7 So¦148158 my fellow¦148159 believers¦148159, be patient¦148157 until¦148160 the return of¦148163 \add Yeshua our\add* \nd master¦148164\nd*. You see how farmers¦148167 look¦148165 forward to the fruit¦148171 to be ready—waiting patiently¦148174 even while they monitor the early¦148184 and¦148185 the late¦148186 rains¦148186.
\v 8 All¦148190 of¦148194 you¦148194 should be patient¦148187 too, and encourage each other \add in your faith\add* because¦148195 the \nd master's¦148199\nd* return is closer now.
\p
\v 9 And don't¦148209 moan about each other, my fellow¦148203 believers¦148203, so that¦148208 you¦148210 all¦148210 won't¦148209 be¦148210 judged¦148210 for it, because truly, the judge¦148214 is just outside about to come in the doors¦148217.
\v 10 Look at the prophets¦148233 who¦148234 spoke¦148235 out the messages from \nd Yahweh¦148239\nd*—they're good examples¦148219 of suffering and¦148228 patience¦148230 \add for you to follow\add*
\v 11 and now we¦148241 consider them as heroes for their endurance. You¦148248 all¦148248 heard¦148248 about¦148247 Yob's¦148247 endurance and then you yourselves witnessed what happened to \add Yeshua our\add* master,\x + \xo 5:11: a \xt Yob 1:21-22; 2:10; \xo b \xt Psa 103:8.\x* and you saw¦148253 his compassion¦148260 and mercy.
\p
\v 12 But¦148288 most importantly, brothers¦148265 and sisters¦148265, don't¦148267 swear¦148268 by heaven¦148271 or earth¦148274 or by any¦148277 other¦148276 kind of¦148284 oath¦148278 but¦148288 simply be¦148286 honest so¦148287 that ‘yes’ means yes and ‘no’ means no,\x + \xo 5:12: \xt Mat 5:34-37.\x* then you¦148297 won't¦148267 end up getting judged¦148296.
\s1 The power of prayer and restoration
